{%- comment -%}
  Handles that must NEVER be used as a product-facing category label — the 22
  industry collections plus the three structural ones.

  Output (comma-wrapped on both sides):
      ,building-construction,display-signage,…,all,frontpage,bestsellers,

  WHY THIS IS A HARD-CODED LIST

  Two earlier attempts derived it from menus and both failed, because on this
  store industries and categories are indistinguishable in the data: all 65
  smart collections use the same rule shape (`tag == own title`), and the main
  menu carries BOTH a Shop tree and an Industries tree, so walking it swept the
  industries straight back in. There is genuinely no signal to infer from.

  So the list is stated outright. It was derived once from the full collection
  list — the 25 collections whose titles contain no product word (tape, tapes,
  dots, dispenser, glue, hang tab, accessories) — minus `strapping-and-filament`,
  which IS a tape category despite its name.

  MAINTENANCE: adding a new industry collection means adding its handle here.
  That is the cost of the trade; the benefit is that it cannot silently break
  again the way the menu-derived versions did.

  Comma-wrapped so a `contains ',handle,'` test cannot match a partial handle
  (`,tape,` must not match `,masking-tape,`).

  Usage — `render` is scope-isolated, so capture it:
      {%- capture skip -%}{% render 'mts-category-handles' %}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign skip = skip | strip -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
